---
/* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Aftercare.

   Closes a real gap: the site previously ended at discharge, and "then what?"
   is a question both patients and families ask when choosing a program.

   Built on CASE MANAGEMENT, which is corroborated on 32 of 571 calls (5.6%) —
   above the working threshold — rather than on the wiki's twelve aftercare
   services, of which almost none is evidenced.

   Corroborating quotes:
     "before she leaves residential, she does have a case manager... they can
      get her all set up with getting a primary care provider, getting a
      psychiatrist, getting a therapist"
     "the case manager will help me find somewhere to go to afterwards"
     "detox should have a case manager or a social worker that talks with the
      client and asks them what they wanna do"
     "the case manager should be able to set her up with medical transport at
      discharge"
     "you work with a case manager to see what your aftercare program is gonna
      look like"

   ⚠ Renamed 2026-09-08: the route was /programs/aftercare-and-alumni/ and the
   nav label was "What happens after". Neither matched how anyone searches, and
   "alumni" in the URL promised services this page deliberately does NOT claim —
   an alumni app, events and reunions appear in 2 calls and none is
   corroborated. Nothing outside navigation.ts and sitemap.astro linked to the
   old path and the branch is unmerged, so no redirect was needed.

   Note the psychiatry line is consistent with the sitewide correction: care is
   ARRANGED for outside, not prescribed here.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TopBar from '../../components/TopBar.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';

import AfterHero from '../../components/after/AfterHero.astro';
import YourCaseManager from '../../components/after/YourCaseManager.astro';
import AfterQuestions from '../../components/after/AfterQuestions.astro';

import Testimonials from '../../components/Testimonials.astro';
import VerifySection from '../../components/VerifySection.astro';
import FinalCTA from '../../components/FinalCTA.astro';
import AdmissionsPath from '../../components/AdmissionsPath.astro';

const title = 'Addiction Aftercare in Chandler, AZ | Buena Vista';
const description =
  'Aftercare planning starts early in your stay: ongoing therapy, a primary care provider, and somewhere to live, arranged before you leave.';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    ['When does discharge planning start at Buena Vista?',
     'Early in the stay rather than the final week. A case manager is assigned in detox and again in residential, and planning for what comes next begins while there is time to arrange it.'],
    ['What is arranged before I leave treatment?',
     'Ongoing therapy, psychiatric care where it applies, a primary care provider, housing if home is not viable, and transport home — so the week after discharge has appointments in it rather than a gap.'],
    ['Does Buena Vista provide outpatient treatment after residential?',
     'Yes. Partial hospitalization, intensive outpatient and outpatient treatment all run at Chandler, so the step down happens in the same building with the same case manager.'],
    ['What happens if I relapse after treatment?',
     'You can call again. Returning is a normal part of recovery for many people and there is no limit on how many times someone can try.'],
  ].map(([q, a]) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a },
  })),
};
---
<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <TopBar />
  <Nav />

  <AfterHero />
  <YourCaseManager />
  <Testimonials />
  <VerifySection
    heading="Does insurance cover aftercare and discharge planning?"
    bullets={[
      'Case management and discharge planning are part of your stay, not an add-on',
      'We check your benefits while you are on the phone, usually in a few minutes',
      'Insurance verification is free and confidential',
      'Not in network with your plan? We will say so, and help you find who is',
    ]}
  />

  <AdmissionsPath
    heading="How to start treatment at Buena Vista"
    bg="bg-white"
    ring="ring-white"
    noteBg="bg-navy-deep"
  />
  <AfterQuestions />

  <FinalCTA />

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} is:inline />
</Layout>
